{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04XQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-groupoids-definition-group-space}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-groupoids-definition-pseudo-torsor}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0002d42c2adc9172acb55958a77085974084083df107126b40344a331769e8cc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:27ca79121ebc0f8861179bb802a1c6177139f825d50fee2e32195e9665e63df0", "source_text": "See\nGroupoids in Spaces,\nDefinitions <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>.\nThe lemma follows immediately from the fact that <MATH_0001> is a\nstack in groupoids.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:80b0b31c94adcf7d95ed5b998ff76408a804eefde33b228c6addd95acae4160a", "unit_id": "tag:04YP:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04XQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\Delta_f :\n\\mathcal{X}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0e64db30e0a88ec5881dd0c1f0cb3b99fff7d22d2433102077a5aa732cfac407", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:13e8b6c5ebbca209882ebc53e91ec0f566f66ec5edba7ffb433729fc070057c3", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>diagonal of <MATH_0002><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is the morphism\n<MATH_0003>\nHere are two properties that every diagonal morphism has.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4227e6a40ee7ae3b05de47077d93848f42b77a041ea99ce22de198ed55cddee1", "unit_id": "tag:04XQ:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04XQ", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{slogan}\nDiagonals of morphisms of algebraic stacks are representable by\nalgebraic spaces and locally of finite type.\n\\end{slogan}", "MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Delta_f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Delta_f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-properties-diagonal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5dfc10e82584660dc049f3560ab6a7038d6398fadc0b299d3ba45c4eb8a78a4e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:086e4d0b8d33f5c3f977b9d8975ad5f5ffae5a865b4737a0ee899d85a0aa6412", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nThen\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is representable by algebraic spaces,\nand\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is locally of finite type.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7f9c4b16c31320a11c3e2be01c44ccdd78d3cbe8fbd5365592cc71b0b30cb3a4", "unit_id": "tag:04XS:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04XQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$a : T \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$2$", "MATH_0004": "$a$", "MATH_0005": "$a = (x, x', \\alpha)$", "MATH_0006": "$x, x'$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0008": "$T$", "MATH_0009": "$\\alpha : f(x) \\to f(x')$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0011": "$T$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathit{Isom}_\\mathcal{X}(x, x')$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathit{Isom}_\\mathcal{Y}(f(x), f(x'))$", "MATH_0014": "$T$", "MATH_0015": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathit{Isom}_\\mathcal{Y}(f(x), f(x')) \\to T$", "MATH_0017": "$T'$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{X} \\times_{\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}, a} T$", "MATH_0019": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0020": "$T$", "MATH_0021": "$x|_{T'} \\to x'|_{T'}$", "MATH_0022": "$f$", "MATH_0023": "$\\alpha|_{T'}$", "MATH_0024": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-diagonal}\n\\vcenter{\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{X} \\times_{\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}, a} T\n\\ar[d] \\ar[r] &\n\\mathit{Isom}_\\mathcal{X}(x, x') \\ar[d] \\\\\nT\\ar[r]^-\\alpha &\n\\mathit{Isom}_\\mathcal{Y}(f(x), f(x'))\n}\n}\n\\end{equation}", "MATH_0025": "$T$", "MATH_0026": "$\\mathcal{X} \\times_{\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}, a} T$", "MATH_0027": "$\\mathit{Isom}_\\mathcal{X}(x, x')$", "MATH_0028": "$T$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-diagonal}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-isom-locally-finite-type}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{equation-diagonal}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-permanence-finite-type}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-base-change-finite-type}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e6c2c11e741e32fd68a93b84cf91d4265aa241adb5e31ad0c4a2fd9ee59009c5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b18b4f77a655f511e13de2ab18804ad57cec014e94c43c3e1198f3e7948277bd", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme and let\n<MATH_0002>\nbe a morphism. By definition of the fibre product and the\n<MATH_0003>-Yoneda lemma the morphism <MATH_0004> is given by a triple\n<MATH_0005> where <MATH_0006> are objects of <MATH_0007>\nover <MATH_0008>, and <MATH_0009> is a morphism in the fibre\ncategory of <MATH_0010> over <MATH_0011>. By definition of an algebraic\nstack the sheaves <MATH_0012> and\n<MATH_0013> are algebraic spaces\nover <MATH_0014>. In this language <MATH_0015> defines a section of the morphism\n<MATH_0016>. A <MATH_0017>-valued point of\n<MATH_0018>\nfor <MATH_0019> a scheme over <MATH_0020> is the same thing as an isomorphism\n<MATH_0021> whose image under <MATH_0022> is <MATH_0023>.\nThus we see that\n<MATH_0024>\nis a fibre square of sheaves over <MATH_0025>. In particular we see that\n<MATH_0026>\nis an algebraic space which proves part (1) of the lemma.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nTo prove the second statement we have to show that the left\nvertical arrow of Diagram (<REF_0001>) is locally\nof finite type. By\nLemma <REF_0002>\nthe algebraic space <MATH_0027>\nis locally of finite type over <MATH_0028>. Hence the right vertical arrow of\nDiagram (<REF_0003>) is locally of finite type, see\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0004>.\nWe conclude by\nMorphisms of Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d6a926b13a3699ef3291bd94d6ab9d9f8543675336d4619849b702189cf92ec9", "unit_id": "tag:04XS:proof"}
